From ca9295d7c2aa9a5bf8cc1ef9524809c8c0380912 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 19:57:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 6: INTERNAL_FLASH_UPDATE_MODE=REMOTE for AS application
 image
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the four AS REMOTE configuration assignments (USE_CONFIGURATION_DEVICE,
CYCLONEIII_CONFIGURATION_DEVICE=EPCS16, CYCLONEIII_CONFIGURATION_SCHEME=
"ACTIVE SERIAL", INTERNAL_FLASH_UPDATE_MODE=REMOTE) so this bitstream
is encoded as a valid AS REMOTE application image.

Context: the neorv32_rot factory bitstream (EPCS page 0) was already built
with INTERNAL_FLASH_UPDATE_MODE=REMOTE so its cycloneive_rublock primitive
can drive pgm_sel and trigger reconfig.  When mode_g wrote a byte-identical
copy of the prior (non-REMOTE) TPU.rbf to EPCS slot 1 @0x80000 and triggered
reconfig, the chip fell back to factory ALINX — the AS controller could not
decode the application image because the non-REMOTE bitstream lacks the
matching configuration-header bits that REMOTE mode requires.

This change does not add new RTL or alter the TPU design; it only changes
the way Quartus encodes the configuration header, so the AS controller in
REMOTE mode will accept the image as a valid application slot.
---
 quartus/neorv32_tpu.qsf | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/quartus/neorv32_tpu.qsf b/quartus/neorv32_tpu.qsf
index 6f7e8e1..84e7f12 100644
--- a/quartus/neorv32_tpu.qsf
+++ b/quartus/neorv32_tpu.qsf
@@ -161,3 +161,15 @@ set_global_assignment -name OPTIMIZATION_MODE "HIGH PERFORMANCE EFFORT"
 set_global_assignment -name PLACEMENT_EFFORT_MULTIPLIER 4.0
 set_global_assignment -name FITTER_EFFORT "STANDARD FIT"
 set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_EFFORT EXTRA
+
+# ── Active Serial REMOTE update — application image at EPCS 0x80000 ─────────
+# Factory bitstream (neorv32_rot) lives at page 0 and uses the cycloneive_rublock
+# primitive to trigger reconfig into this TPU image at slot 1.  Both factory
+# and application images must be compiled with INTERNAL_FLASH_UPDATE_MODE=REMOTE
+# so the AS configuration controller honours the rublock-driven pgm_sel and
+# decodes the application image with the matching watchdog / page-select bits.
+# Quartus 21.1 uses CYCLONEIII_* assignment names for the Cyclone IV E family.
+set_global_assignment -name USE_CONFIGURATION_DEVICE ON
+set_global_assignment -name CYCLONEIII_CONFIGURATION_DEVICE EPCS16
+set_global_assignment -name CYCLONEIII_CONFIGURATION_SCHEME "ACTIVE SERIAL"
+set_global_assignment -name INTERNAL_FLASH_UPDATE_MODE "REMOTE"
-- 
